  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Greetings,\nYou are always quick to respond to bugs and add new features, and we can't thank you enough.\nNow, on the subject at hand, I would like to propose to open up the limit on the number of bits in the exp-parameter.\nMore and more systems are consuming richer bits these days, and combined with my own personal development gimmicks, I can easily break the 128-bit limit.\nI've managed to cope with this by splitting and omitting functions, but I'm wondering if it would be possible to consolidate these problems into one avatar, which would not only solve these problems, but also reduce the number of files stored on the server.\nI'm sure there are some difficulties in dealing with Quest, so if it's possible, that's fine.\nPlease consider implementing this in the future.\nThank you for reading this long article.",
